---
// Questions people ask before installing an unofficial player. Native <details> in one named
// group, so one answer is open at a time, it works without script and with the keyboard,
// and every one starts closed. Where the browser can, an answer opens and closes by easing
// its height (::details-content); elsewhere it simply appears. Facts from the repo's README.
import { repo } from "../data/links";
const faqs = [
  {
    id: "official",
    q: "Is featherplay official?",
    a: [
      "No. featherplay is an independent, unofficial player for YouTube Music. It isn't made by Google or YouTube and isn't affiliated with them.",
      "Because it's unofficial, a change on YouTube's side can break playback until featherplay is updated. If something stops working, update first.",
    ],
  },
  {
    q: "How does signing in work?",
    a: [
      "featherplay opens a small sign-in window, Microsoft Edge WebView2, with Google's own sign-in page. You sign in there as you would in a browser. featherplay doesn't read your password; the code is open. Once you're in, it keeps the YouTube Music session from that window and closes it. The main window never contains a browser.",
      "If you'd rather sign in in a browser you know, choose Sign in with Microsoft Edge. Edge opens with a temporary profile, with its own address bar, passkeys and Windows Hello. featherplay keeps only the YouTube Music session from it, then closes Edge and deletes the profile. Your own Edge profile is never touched.",
      "The session is kept in Windows Credential Manager, never in a file. It gives the same access to your account as a signed-in browser, so treat it like a password; Sign out in Settings removes it. Windows 11 includes WebView2, and most Windows 10 PCs have it with Edge.",
    ],
  },
  {
    q: "Is my account safe with it?",
    a: [
      "Your YouTube Music session, your Last.fm session and your ListenBrainz token stay on your PC, in Windows Credential Manager. The code is public for anyone to read.",
      "It is still an unofficial client, using YouTube Music in a way Google doesn't support. If that worries you, sign in with a second account.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "connects",
    q: "What does it connect to?",
    a: [
      "featherplay sends no telemetry and has no server of its own. It connects to YouTube Music and Google for your music, covers, streams and sign-in, and to GitHub to fetch yt-dlp and Deno on the first run and to update yt-dlp.",
      "LRCLIB gets the song's title, artist, album and length, only while lyrics are on screen. SponsorBlock, on by default, is asked only about music videos and uploads (songs have nothing to skip), by the first four characters of a hash of the video's ID, so it doesn't learn which video you play.",
      "Last.fm and ListenBrainz hear from it only if you connect them, and Discord only if you turn on the status, through the Discord app on your own PC.",
    ],
  },
  {
    q: "Does it download anything else?",
    a: [
      "Yes, two helpers, on the first run: yt-dlp, which finds each song's audio stream, and Deno, which yt-dlp needs to do it. featherplay fetches both from their GitHub releases and checks each file against a SHA256 written into its own code; a file that doesn't match is deleted, not run.",
      "After that it updates yt-dlp at most once a day, because YouTube changes often. Nothing else is downloaded, and never the music itself.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "uninstall",
    q: "How do I uninstall it?",
    a: [
      "Installed: uninstall it from Settings > Apps. That removes everything featherplay keeps: settings, cache, the helpers, the sign-in window's data and its entries in Credential Manager.",
      "Portable: sign out and disconnect Last.fm in Settings first, which clears both from Credential Manager. Then delete the exe and its two folders, %APPDATA%\\featherplay and %LOCALAPPDATA%\\featherplay.",
    ],
  },
  {
    q: "Why only Windows?",
    a: [
      "featherplay is built on Windows' own parts: the media overlay, the taskbar buttons, the notification area and Credential Manager. That's a lot of what keeps it light. There's no macOS or Linux version.",
    ],
  },
  {
    q: "Is it free?",
    a: ["Yes. It's free and open source under the MIT licence, with no paid tier and no account to create."],
  },
  {
    q: "How do I report a bug?",
    a: [`Open an issue on GitHub. Say what you did, what you expected and what happened, and add the version from Settings, About.`],
    link: { href: `${repo}/issues`, text: "Open an issue on GitHub" },
  },
];
---

<section id="questions" class="faq" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div class="intro">
      <h2 id="questions-title">Questions</h2>
      <p class="aside">
        Something else? <a href={`${repo}/issues`}>Ask on GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="list" data-faq>
      {
        faqs.map((f) => (
          <details name="faq" id={f.id}>
            <summary>
              <span class="q">{f.q}</span>
              <span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18">
                  <path d="M12 6 V18 M6 12 H18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" />
                </svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="answer">
              {f.a.map((p) => (
                <p>{p}</p>
              ))}
              {f.link && (
                <p>
                  <a href={f.link.href}>{f.link.text}</a>
                </p>
              )}
            </div>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  // A link to a question (the footer's Help and Legal links: #official, #connects, #uninstall) opens its answer.
  const openTarget = () => {
    const id = decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1));
    const target = id ? document.getElementById(id) : null;
    if (target instanceof HTMLDetailsElement && target.closest("[data-faq]")) target.open = true;
  };
  addEventListener("hashchange", openTarget);
  openTarget();
</script>

<style>
  .faq {
    padding-block: clamp(96px, 11vw, 180px);
  }
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: var(--split);
    gap: var(--split-gap);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .intro {
    position: sticky;
    top: 112px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 4.6vw, 4.25rem);
  }
  .aside {
    max-width: 28ch;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .aside a,
  .answer a {
    font-weight: 700;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  /* The list: rows on the page's own ground; the open one rises a tone. */
  .list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  details {
    border-radius: 20px;
    transition: background-color calc(240ms * var(--colour-easing)) ease;
  }
  details[open] {
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 24px;
    min-height: 80px;
    padding: 20px 20px 20px 24px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    transition: background-color var(--t-hover) ease;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  @media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
    details:not([open]) summary:hover {
      background: var(--hover);
    }
  }
  .q {
    font-size: clamp(1.1875rem, 1.7vw, 1.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .mark {
    display: grid;
    flex: none;
    place-items: center;
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--selected);
    transition:
      transform 260ms var(--ease-out),
      background-color calc(240ms * var(--colour-easing)) ease;
  }
  details[open] .mark {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }
  .answer {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    max-width: 62ch;
    padding: 0 24px 26px;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* The height eases open and shut where the browser can animate to auto. */
  @supports selector(::details-content) {
    .list {
      interpolate-size: allow-keywords;
    }
    details::details-content {
      block-size: 0;
      overflow: clip;
      transition:
        block-size 280ms var(--ease-out),
        content-visibility 280ms allow-discrete;
    }
    details[open]::details-content {
      block-size: auto;
    }
    .answer {
      opacity: 0;
      transition: opacity 200ms ease;
    }
    details[open] .answer {
      opacity: 1;
      transition-delay: 60ms;
    }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    details::details-content {
      transition: none;
    }
    .mark {
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .intro {
      position: static;
    }
    summary {
      padding-inline: 16px 12px;
    }
    .answer {
      padding-inline: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
